   "notes": "St Catharine's College range on the west side of Trumpington Street (street front between the stone Bull building to the north and King's Lane side): mostly a three-storey red-brick Georgian-style range with stone architraves to the sashes, stone plinth and cornice, and a row of dormers; at the south end a narrow stone-faced bay with a curved pedimented gable. Positions are rough from two oblique Mapillary views looking south along Trumpington Street."
